{"id": "EUVD-2026-76585", "enisaUuid": "072d2ea7-f31a-3e3c-b653-da92298a7be9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: fix XDR padding calculation in ff_encode_getdeviceinfo\n\nnfsd4_ff_encode_getdeviceinfo() computes the da_addr_body reservation\nas 16 + netid_len + addr_len, but the subsequent xdr_encode_opaque()\ncalls emit 8 + round_up(netid_len, 4) + round_up(addr_len, 4) bytes.\nThe mismatch means the declared da_addr_body length exceeds the actual\nencoded data by 2-8 bytes on every flexfile GETDEVICEINFO reply,\nleaking stale reply-page content to the client and mis-aligning the\nsubsequent version list decode.\n\nUse xdr_align_size() for each string length to match what\nxdr_encode_opaque() actually writes.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:50:46", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88bce7e326c368d7df15126ccac537e54bebd467", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/74015b7be806ad9e21d46f7bd2831df280c6c783", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/41ebca28e17f84293650598f86bd69532ec1a8e0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/62e5949f0dd5ec837af144860ff908369df4c7c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8b989aaec85e1293a871d602590c951fe44b8647"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89673", "GHSA-fpgc-gpfg-74f9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16ee56f0-ea25-377b-9473-a7f7f88a98df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4.16 <6.18.50"}, {"id": "1eb951e6-42c6-3acf-8bc2-a977faef358f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4.16 <6.6.157"}, {"id": "3843c956-d576-378c-b065-7615be501479", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "efcae97fa425ca6db9d126e37daccf2d7225cb09 <74015b7be806ad9e21d46f7bd2831df280c6c783"}, {"id": "44a96ae6-89cf-330e-901e-d7c73aff0c5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4.16 <7.3"}, {"id": "70cb250d-baab-38da-b91a-20016177bf74", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4.16 <6.12.109"}, {"id": "8b1d7f94-8246-3319-9301-596ed7dd3076", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "efcae97fa425ca6db9d126e37daccf2d7225cb09 <41ebca28e17f84293650598f86bd69532ec1a8e0"}, {"id": "a64a14b2-0309-3321-8235-8835d706b588", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "efcae97fa425ca6db9d126e37daccf2d7225cb09 <62e5949f0dd5ec837af144860ff908369df4c7c9"}, {"id": "a9d3b94c-7ad8-33a6-9c96-1dfda62b64e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "efcae97fa425ca6db9d126e37daccf2d7225cb09 <8b989aaec85e1293a871d602590c951fe44b8647"}, {"id": "c5b06523-f16d-3c30-900a-91a508ff01db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "efcae97fa425ca6db9d126e37daccf2d7225cb09 <88bce7e326c368d7df15126ccac537e54bebd467"}, {"id": "d4551dc9-2ca8-3422-a830-a987190febba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4.16 <7.2.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "234be652-e5f7-34c6-9bd9-eac1247bb028", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}